{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/e/c3e80df820ca1f77534888f61935a55d0b6ec94f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z), Q(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"85\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a3bd8ec8295d5ebd0a199f4c3d5c71f36ba8455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> are polynomials with real coefficients, having degrees <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, respectively, and constant terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of distinct complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc003aaa5cf7c3992be4089e21fb98b51b3ce54b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z) \\cdot Q(z)=R(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"152\" height=\"20\" />. What is the minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/b/04bd2f01cecd7ac0b50ba3fe36bace3498400490.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\: 0\\qquad\\textbf{(B)} \\: 1\\qquad\\textbf{(C)} \\: 2\\qquad\\textbf{(D)} \\: 3\\qquad\\textbf{(E)} \\: 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"344\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The answer cannot be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/d/ced6b9b2e75857b566f1e516560c4a4d63977299.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> as every nonconstant polynomial has at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> distinct complex root (Fundamental Theorem of Algebra). Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/3/ff3700d94970038b2e96b85d7815675a434e7f86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(z) \\cdot Q(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> has degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/65436d552dbec71bdbb6b9f6c197e10f4bcc482c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 + 3 = 5,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"17\" /> we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74fcf43a5597fa2227b53a49c21e75716b0765f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(z) - P(z)\\cdot Q(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" /> has degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and is thus nonconstant.\n</p><p>It now suffices to illustrate an example for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/3/b7331aa4b5e853bc095a9a02277bbb1e6a7a84d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" />: Take\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/3/493c2295ed92460a75965adfbaafe893c51f3f3d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} P(z)&amp;=z^2+1, \\\\ Q(z)&amp;=z^3+2, \\\\ R(z)&amp;=(z+1)^6 + P(z) \\cdot Q(z). \\end{align*}\" width=\"238\" height=\"75\" />\nNote that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/3/5a3bd8ec8295d5ebd0a199f4c3d5c71f36ba8455.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R(z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> has degree <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and constant term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f885f96d2fb7e65f800de4ff71d7dcd0a5d2db5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"16\" /> so it satisfies the conditions.\n</p><p>We need to find the solutions to \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/8/aa8fdf38114e1f311a2baacd752f81fa04bcb7cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} P(z) \\cdot Q(z) &amp;= (z+1)^6 + P(z) \\cdot Q(z) \\\\ 0 &amp;= (z+1)^6. \\end{align*}\" width=\"283\" height=\"47\" />\nClearly, the only distinct complex root is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/9/7499fffa6a36b9e00d7c4209dad1813ae7167a1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be2ab6e3cbdaa781c1640676546af3a63565acd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\: 1}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"101\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~kingofpineapplz ~kgator\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/HLhetkPGfX4\">https://youtu.be/HLhetkPGfX4</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B\">2021 Fall AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-